course: dictionary
lesson: 1699
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Church can mean three different things, and the words around it show you which one. «We go to church on Sunday» means the service held there. Here, church is something that happens, not a place.
explain: «Turn left at the church, then walk past the shop.» Church means the building, and the clue is turn left and walk past. People use a church as a landmark to find their way.
explain: «Paul wrote letters to churches» means groups of Christians who met together in towns long ago, not buildings. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? A group of people fits, so that is the meaning.
fact: A church is a building where Christians go to pray and worship.
fact: Church can also mean a group of Christians who share the same beliefs, like the Catholic Church.
fact: Church can mean the service held there: «We go to church on Sunday.»
fact: Churches often have a tower, a spire or bells, so you can spot them from a long way off.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «We go to church on Sunday.» In this sentence, church means: | A shop where you buy bread | A group of friends from school | *The service held there | A tall tower with bells
exercise: «The church bells rang out at noon.» Which word is a clue that church means the building? | *bells | out | rang | noon
exercise: «Paul wrote letters to churches.» What does churches mean here? | Services held on Sunday | Choirs who sing hymns | Buildings with tall spires | *Groups of Christians who meet together
test: «The Catholic Church has members in many countries.» What does Church mean here? | A Sunday service | *A group of Christians who share the same beliefs | A building with a tower | A school hall
test: «Baptists and many Pentecostal churches baptise people old enough to decide.» In this sentence, churches means: | Shops that sell candles | Towers with bells that ring | Buildings for school lessons | *Groups of Christians with their own beliefs
exam: «Turn left at the church, then walk past the shop.» Why is the church useful here, and what does it mean? | A group of people who walk together | *A building people use as a guide to find the way | A Sunday service in the street | A shop that sells bread
